{"kind":"assert","text":"Bounded security task-selection audit at Main 132a5e2afe9cdfddbc81ed434eb9a6dbd48ca2b6 (tree ecb704172ff78ffe6fbbb6de8c0bad7fe69f9057). R16 is the earliest genuinely unfinished independently implementable task after the landed D1/D2 and R1–R3/R8/R12 work. Its later explicit ordering is after R8 and before R5, overriding any inference that R5's original order 5/10 comes next. Existing request b300dca1381f27beed6c0d3278ccc5955f86c7dc and implementation promise d107501f110b3999dded992f08676cf0722243b6 remain promised. The promise begins with source inventory/design and does not supply implementation evidence.\n\nCurrent Source demonstrates the real gap: packages/bytes/src/edit-path.ts:11–14 rejects malformed components and .git, but accepts .github and ordinary control-file names; packages/platform/src/destination.ts:2592–2595 admits publish-file, and fileJudge at 2663–2679 checks syntax/present and constructs the publication without reserved/prefix policy. packages/scope/src/destination-host.ts:522–536 constructs the supplied file path without an application-prefix/reserved check. ApplicationSemantics at packages/bytes/src/application-types.ts:18–29 and its v2 extension at application-v2-types.ts:13–16 contain no publication-prefix declaration. The existing fold note explicitly permits rules-extent overwrites at notes/2026-10-13-fold-publication.md:371–377. These are bounded positive Source findings, not a claimed exhaustive exploit audit.\n\nThe accepted ruling d31ea3d2 fixes the implementation constraints: reserve .github, any-depth AGENTS.md/CLAUDE.md, Git controls, current authority/rules controls and effective symlink paths while ordinary content remains writable; check declared prefixes at install and publication; add a new Destination version without changing old pinned rules; old pinned hosts record their existing truthful refusal representation. Legacy Lending compatibility is a finite map bound to exact approved signed-release and definition pins for shelf/, never a name/global default; unknown or missing declarations otherwise fail closed. Next Lending release declares shelf/ and planner removes that map when moved. Grow declares none. Exact approved compatibility pins and the complete reserved-file/read-site inventory must be bound during implementation; this audit invents neither. Checker review each head, one final-head gate, hosted Workers remain deployable, planner deploys and builder does not; archive work retains priority. Required witnesses include reserved workflow/rules refusal in new rules and old host, allowed-prefix commit, reserved-prefix install refusal, Lending continuity and unchanged pinned replay.\n\nAdministrative distinction: the visible R1/R2/R3/R8/R12 parent commitments still project promised, but accepted Main includes f7b59bf92d1abe20300818ab109fa12df617c2e0 and its documented integrated admission/index/serving/sandbox/key work. Their status alone is not an instruction to reimplement or rerun them. D1/D2 earlier landings also precede this Main. This assertion neither closes those parents nor claims hosted/operator obligations complete. R5 remains a real later task (8a856f92d974caf28f09375f3973726f4d7377b7); its e6336adf9ffe49356d92642357b41401f242ed59 promise is explicitly reconnaissance only, and R15 is ordered with it. Subsequent original groups remain R9/R10/R11, R4/R13, R6/R7, D3–D6 and R14. No promises, closures, ratifications, Source/ref changes, tests or runtime were performed by this audit."}